wireguard — provenance note
===========================

A record only. Nothing in this file imposes a redistribution condition beyond
zig-libs' own MIT license (see the repository `LICENSE`). Moved here from the
root `NOTICE` §2 on 2026-08-14, unchanged in substance.

Kernel UAPI (clean-room)
------------------------

Original pure-Zig reimplementation of the WireGuard netlink protocol from the
documented UAPI headers (`uapi/wireguard.h`; **GPL-2.0 WITH
Linux-syscall-note**). No GPL header source is copied — only the
uncopyrightable ABI facts they document are used (command/attribute/flag
constants, struct layouts).

The operative mechanism is the Linux-syscall-note exception itself: it
explicitly states that using these headers to make syscalls / interface with
the kernel does not bring the resulting work under the GPL, for userspace of
ANY license — which is why this module is cleanly MIT despite citing GPL-2.0
headers.

The generic-netlink transport (`genlmsghdr` + `nlctrl` family resolve) this
module sits on is the `genetlink` module — see its own provenance note.

