Black-box test oracles
----------------------

The real `wg`(8) binary (wireguard-tools, **GPL-2.0**) and the real kernel
`wireguard.ko` module were run ONLY as black-box test oracles under `strace`
inside a throwaway network namespace, their request/reply bytes frozen and
diffed against this module's own codec — no `wg`/kernel source consulted,
studied or ported (`kernel_goldens.zig`).

Reserved Noise_IKpsk2 handshake
-------------------------------

The same module's `noise.zig`/`handshake.zig` (currently a compiling scaffold,
no crypto implemented — see those files' own doc-comments) reserve the
Noise_IKpsk2 cryptographic handshake: clean-room from the WireGuard protocol
whitepaper (J. A. Donenfeld, "WireGuard: Next Generation Kernel Network
Tunnel", NDSS 2017, wireguard.com/papers/wireguard.pdf, and
wireguard.com/protocol/) and the Noise Protocol Framework spec
(noiseprotocol.org, pattern IKpsk2).

Design reference: wireguard-go (`golang.zx2c4.com/wireguard`, **MIT**) and the
Linux kernel WireGuard implementation (**GPL-2.0**) — message layout /
handshake step order only (the standardized wire protocol, not copyrightable
expression); no source consulted or copied.
